{
  "_": [
    "Story two, same machinery. Twelve narration segments, twelve shots.",
    "",
    "The structural invariant here is the RIDE group, not the carry group: the monkey sits",
    "on the crocodile's back, at a saddle point measured off the crocodile's own drawing.",
    "He cannot drift off it, sink into it, or end up behind the animal he is riding.",
    "",
    "THE WIFE IS NEVER DRAWN. She wants to eat the monkey's heart, and she is the reason",
    "the story happens -- but the app's telling keeps her a voice from off the page, and",
    "docs/14 says harm stays as elliptical on the channel as it is in the text. So the",
    "evening shots are the crocodile alone with what he has been asked to do, which is",
    "also the more interesting picture."
  ],
